The attached image, Fig. 2 (A) and (B) from the PDF, illustrates the physical characterization of Nano-11 nanoparticles. Panel (A) is a Transmission Electron Microscopy image showing spherical particles with an irregular, cauliflower-like appearance, mostly single or in pairs, with a 50 nm scale bar. Panel (B) displays the particle size distribution determined by dynamic light scattering, indicating a Z-average hydrodynamic diameter ranging from 75 to 80 nm, with particles generally uniform in size from 30 to 110 nm. This characterization confirms the nanoscale dimensions and morphology of the adjuvant.